Endpoint What it does <code>POST /v1/files</code> upload one file (<code>{filename, media_type, data_base64}</code>) as an artifact <code>GET /v1/artifacts/{id}</code> download an artifact's bytes (recorded media type) <code>GET /v1/artifacts/{id}/meta</code> the artifact's <code>ArtifactRef</code> <p><code>POST /v1/files</code> uploads one file as an artifact (<code>{filename, media_type, data_base64}</code>, strict JSON) and returns the full record:</p> <pre><code>{"id": "art_…", "media_type": "text/plain", "filename": "report.txt",
 "size": 1842, "sha256": "…", "source": "user", "turn_id": null,
 "session_id": null, "created_at": "…", "url": "/v1/artifacts/art_…"}
</code></pre> <pre><code>$ B64=$(base64 -w0 report.txt)
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11440/v1/files \
    -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
    -d "{\"filename\": \"report.txt\", \"media_type\": \"text/plain\",
         \"data_base64\": \"$B64\"}"
{"id": "art_…", "url": "/v1/artifacts/art_…", …}

$ curl -s -o report.txt http://127.0.0.1:11440/v1/artifacts/art_…   # download
$ curl -s http://127.0.0.1:11440/v1/artifacts/art_…/meta           # the ref
</code></pre> <p>Messages reference it as <code>{"type": "file", "file_id": "art_…"}</code> — in agent-turn content arrays and in OpenAI messages alike; a missing or expired id is a structured <code>404 artifact_not_found</code> before inference:</p> <pre><code>{"role": "user", "content": [
  {"type": "text", "text": "Summarize this report"},
  {"type": "file", "file_id": "art_…"}
]}
</code></pre>
